  <h2>💬 How to Select Models via Chat</h2>
  <p>
    You can query any specific model or use intelligent shortcut commands:
  </p>

  <pre><code># 1. Quick Shortcut for Google Gemini Flash:
/gemini Explain how systemd timers compare to crond

# 2. Quick Shortcut for GitHub GPT-4o:
/gpt4 Write a TypeScript interface for this JSON schema

# 3. Model Flag Selection via /chat:
/chat -m reasoning-heavy Optimize this SQL join query for 10M rows
/chat -m coder-smart Find and fix the memory leak in worker.py

# 4. Interactive Dashboard:
/models     # Displays active models with tap-to-ask inline action buttons!
/modelhelp  # Displays in-depth model documentation inside chat</code></pre>

  <h2>🔄 Redundancy & Failover Configuration</h2>
  <p>
    The LiteLLM gateway configuration lives in <code>litellm/config.yaml</code> at the root of your Agent Station install, mounted read-only into the <code>litellm-proxy</code> container at <code>/app/config.yaml</code>. The excerpts below are copied verbatim from that file so they can't silently drift from what's actually deployed -- a CI check fails the build if they ever stop matching.
  </p>
  <p>
    First two deployments of the <code>coder-fast</code> pool (free OpenRouter models are listed first in every router; see <a href="#free-tier-models-via-openrouter">Free-Tier Models via OpenRouter</a> below for the full per-router breakdown):
  </p>

  <pre><code>  - model_name: coder-fast
    litellm_params:
      model: openrouter/nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free
      api_key: os.environ/OPENROUTER_API_KEY
  - model_name: coder-fast
    litellm_params:
      model: openrouter/poolside/laguna-xs-2.1:free
      api_key: os.environ/OPENROUTER_API_KEY</code></pre>

  <p>The router-level settings, applied to every virtual router above:</p>

  <pre><code>router_settings:
  routing_strategy: usage-based-routing
  set_verbose: false
  num_retries: 3
  timeout: 120
  retry_after: 5
  cooldown_time: 30 # Cooldown provider for 30s when a 429 occurs
  allowed_fails: 2
  fallbacks:
    - coder-smart: ["gemini-3.7-pro", "gemini-3.7-flash", "github-gpt-4o", "gemini-2.5-flash"]
    - coder-fast: ["gemini-3.7-flash", "gemini-2.5-flash", "github-gpt-4o"]
    - reasoning-heavy: ["gemini-3.7-pro", "github-deepseek-r1", "github-o3-mini", "gemini-3.7-flash"]
    - claude-3-7-sonnet-direct: ["gemini-3.7-pro", "github-gpt-4o", "gemini-3.7-flash"]
    - claude-3-7-sonnet-vertex: ["gemini-3.7-pro", "github-gpt-4o", "gemini-3.7-flash"]
    - gemini-3.7-pro: ["gemini-3.7-flash", "github-gpt-4o", "gemini-2.5-flash"]
    - gemini-3.7-flash: ["gemini-2.5-flash", "github-gpt-4o"]</code></pre>

  <h2 id="free-tier-models-via-openrouter">🆓 Free-Tier Models via OpenRouter</h2>
  <div class="docs-callout docs-callout-info">
    Setting <code>OPENROUTER_API_KEY</code> (get one at <a href="https://openrouter.ai/keys" target="_blank" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">openrouter.ai/keys</a>) unlocks a $0-cost tier tried <em>before</em> Gemini/Claude/GPT-4o in every router above. It's optional, purely additive, and safe to enable -- without the key those deployments just fail instantly and the router falls through to the paid tiers exactly as before.
  </div>
  <table class="docs-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Virtual Router</th>
        <th>Free OpenRouter Deployments (tried first)</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>coder-fast</code></td>
        <td><code>nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning:free</code>, <code>poolside/laguna-xs-2.1:free</code></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>coder-smart</code></td>
        <td><code>poolside/laguna-s-2.1:free</code>, <code>cohere/north-mini-code:free</code>, <code>nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free</code></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>reasoning-heavy</code></td>
        <td><code>z-ai/glm-5.2:free</code>, <code>nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free</code></td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    <strong>Tradeoff:</strong> free models carry tighter rate limits and are generally lower quality for hard agentic coding tasks than the paid deployments they sit in front of -- LiteLLM's cooldown logic skips a failing/rate-limited one automatically, so the practical cost is occasionally weaker answers rather than downtime.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>This is a point-in-time snapshot:</strong> OpenRouter adds and retires free models over time. To re-check what's currently free, query <a href="https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models" target="_blank" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models</a> and filter for entries where <code>pricing.prompt == "0"</code>, then compare against <code>litellm/config.yaml</code>.
  </p>
